# Engram memory is on

You have persistent memory of the user through the `engram` MCP server. Follow
the `engram-memory` skill:

- At the start of a conversation, resolve the workspace and user peer and call
  `get_peer_context` for the user. Act on what it says.
- When past context would help, use `search` or `chat` instead of asking the
  user to repeat themselves.
- After every exchange, record the user's message and your reply with
  `add_messages_to_session`, unless the session-start context says automatic
  capture is on, in which case the hooks already did. Replace secrets with
  `[redacted]`.
- When the user states a durable preference, store it with
  `create_conclusions`.

If a Engram tool returns an authentication error, run the `engram-setup`
skill instead of retrying.
